    <detaileddescription>
<para>This example shows how to perform training and how to predict with a trained model.</para>
<para>To compile with <computeroutput>g++</computeroutput> and run:</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".sh"><codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>g++<sp/>-O3<sp/>ex1.cpp<sp/>-o<sp/>ex1.out<sp/>-ltadah<sp/>-fopenmp</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">$<sp/>./ex1.out</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Ta-dah! models and descriptors are selected at compile time but all model parameters are provided in the config file.</para>
<para>Here we use Blip2B two-body descriptor and train using both energies and virial stresses.</para>
<para>Files:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="ex1_8cpp" kindref="compound">ex1.cpp</ref></computeroutput> Example c++ script for training and prediction.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>config</computeroutput> <ref refid="classConfig" kindref="compound">Config</ref> file used for training, contains all model parameters.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>config_pred</computeroutput> List of datasets used for prediction (<ref refid="classConfig_1DBFILE" kindref="member">DBFILE</ref> key). Keys <ref refid="classConfig_1FORCE" kindref="member">FORCE</ref> and <ref refid="classConfig_1STRESS" kindref="member">STRESS</ref> controls whether forces and stresses are predicted.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>tdata.db</computeroutput> Dataset which we will use for both training and prediction. The dataset is generated using EAM model for Ta by R.Ravelo. <ulink url="https://journals.aps.org/prb/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevB.88.134101">https://journals.aps.org/prb/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevB.88.134101</ulink> </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
